# Bench units: get adb authorized again after a factory reset, with nobody at
# the screen. A wipe takes /data/misc/adb/adb_keys with it, so every reflash
# with --wipe used to need a hand on the phone to tap "Allow USB debugging".
#
# A unit is opted in by putting a host key list at
# /mnt/vendor/persist/pepito/adb_keys (scripts/setup-phone.sh --enroll, which
# needs an already-authorized, rooted adb). /persist survives the wipe; on the
# first boot after it, this copies that list into the file adbd reads. A unit
# without the file (every user's phone) gets a failed copy and nothing else.
# Removing the file un-enrolls (setup-phone.sh --unenroll): do it before a
# unit is sold.
#
# Once per wipe, not every boot: persist.vendor.xiaomi.adbkeys_seeded lives in
# /data/property, so it is unset exactly when /data is fresh, and keys added
# later through the dialog are not overwritten at the next reboot. Fires when
# the persist props have loaded, after init.usb.rc has made /data/misc/adb.
#
# system_ext, NOT vendor: adb_keys_file is a core_data_file_type, which
# vendor_init may not write (see init.pepito-sensors.rc). Debuggable builds
# only: a user build has no business trusting a key planted outside the dialog.
on property:ro.persistent_properties.ready=true && property:ro.debuggable=1 && property:ro.vendor.xiaomi.device=pepito && property:persist.vendor.xiaomi.adbkeys_seeded=
    mkdir /data/misc/adb 02750 system shell
    copy /mnt/vendor/persist/pepito/adb_keys /data/misc/adb/adb_keys
    chown system shell /data/misc/adb/adb_keys
    chmod 0640 /data/misc/adb/adb_keys
    setprop persist.vendor.xiaomi.adbkeys_seeded 1
